LESSON 11 — Nested Functions

A function can be defined inside another function.

Think of a hospital.

Hospital
    ├── Reception
    ├── Pharmacy
    └── Billing

The hospital controls all three departments.

Similarly,

Main Function
    ├── Inner Function
    ├── Inner Function
Example 1
def hospital():

    def reception():
        print("Patient Registration")

    reception()

hospital()

Output

Patient Registration

Notice

hospital()
      |
      +---- reception()

The inner function cannot be called directly.

reception()

Output

NameError

because it exists only inside hospital().
